{{define "index"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main">
<p class="pitch hot">An arcade in your terminal. Free play.</p>
<div class="floor">
  <div class="list">
    <p class="cmd"><span class="dim">$</span> ls -l /usr/games</p>
{{range .Games}}    <a class="row" href="/{{.Name}}{{if index $.Play .Name}}#play{{end}}"><span class="perm" aria-hidden="true">-rwxr-xr-x</span><span class="own" aria-hidden="true">root</span><span class="grp" aria-hidden="true">games</span><span>{{.Players}}</span><span>{{.Name}}(6)</span></a>
{{end}}    <p class="hint dim">{{.Count}} Up and down to choose, return to play.<span class="cursor blink"></span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="preview">
{{if .Rec}}    <input type="checkbox" id="hold" class="hold">
{{end}}{{range $i, $g := .Games}}    <div class="att"{{if $i}} hidden{{end}}>
      {{template "screen" (screen $g (index $.Rec $g.Name))}}
      <img class="name" src="/media/{{$g.Name}}/name.svg" alt="{{$g.Name}}(6)" width="{{namew $g.Name 3}}" height="80">
      <p class="dim">{{$g.Blurb}}</p>
      <p><a class="rev" href="/{{$g.Name}}{{if index $.Play $g.Name}}#play{{end}}">&nbsp;Play&nbsp;</a> <span class="blink">or press return</span></p>
    </div>
{{end}}{{if .Rec}}    <label for="hold" class="hold">pause</label>
{{end}}  </div>
  <div class="homecol">
    <section>
      <h2>Play it here, or take it home.</h2>
      <p><span class="dim">$</span> curl -fsSL https://usr.games/install.sh | sh</p>
      <p><span class="dim">$</span> tty1</p>
      <p class="dim note"><a href="/tty1">tty1</a> is the launcher. It installs the games, keeps them current, and starts them.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2><a href="/terminals">Bring a good terminal.</a></h2>
      <p class="dim">Best in Ghostty, kitty, WezTerm, foot or iTerm2. Apple's Terminal works, with one key held at a time.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "game"}}{{template "head" .}}<nav class="names" aria-label="The games">
  <p class="dim">$ ls /usr/games</p>
  {{template "games" .}}
</nav>
<main id="main" class="page">
  <div class="att" id="play"{{with index .Play .Game.Name}} data-name="{{$.Game.Name}}" data-game="/play/{{$.Game.Name}}/{{.}}/{{$.Game.Name}}.wasm.gz" data-exec="/play/{{$.Game.Name}}/{{.}}/wasm_exec.js" data-player="{{$.Player}}" data-cols="{{index $.Game.PlaySize 0}}" data-rows="{{index $.Game.PlaySize 1}}"{{end}}>{{if index .Rec .Game.Name}}<input type="checkbox" id="hold" class="hold">{{end}}{{template "screen" (screen .Game (index .Rec .Game.Name))}}{{if index .Rec .Game.Name}}<label for="hold" class="hold">pause</label>{{end}}</div>
  <div class="side">
    <div>
      <h1 class="title"><img src="/media/{{.Game.Name}}/name.svg" alt="{{.Game.Name}}(6)" width="{{namew .Game.Name 3}}" height="80"></h1>
      <p class="about">{{.Game.About}}</p>
      <p class="dim">{{.Game.Facts}}</p>
    </div>
    <section>
      <h2>Keys</h2>
      <dl class="keys">{{range .Game.Keys}}<dt>{{index . 0}}</dt><dd class="dim">{{index . 1}}</dd>{{end}}</dl>
{{if index .Man .Game.Name}}      <p class="dim note">Every key and option is in <a href="/man/{{.Game.Name}}">its manual page</a>.</p>
{{end}}    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Take it home</h2>
      <p><span class="dim">$</span> tty1 install {{.Game.Name}}</p>
      <p><span class="dim">$</span> tty1 man {{.Game.Name}}</p>
    </section>
{{if .Others}}    <section>
      <h2>See also</h2>
      <p>{{range $i, $g := .Others}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}<a href="/{{$g.Name}}">{{$g.Name}}(6)</a>{{end}}</p>
    </section>
{{end}}  </div>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "tty1"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main" class="doc">
  <div>
    <h1 class="title"><img src="/media/tty1/name.svg" alt="tty1" width="{{namew "tty1" 0}}" height="80"></h1>
    <p class="about">tty1 is the launcher: one command that installs the games, keeps them current, and starts them.</p>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Get it</h2>
    <p><span class="dim">$</span> curl -fsSL https://usr.games/install.sh | sh</p>
    <p><span class="dim">$</span> go install usr.games/tty1@latest</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use it</h2>
    <dl class="keys wide"><dt>tty1 ls</dt><dd class="dim">list the games</dd><dt>tty1 install {{.Example}}</dt><dd class="dim">bring a game home</dd><dt>tty1 update</dt><dd class="dim">bring everything up to date</dd><dt>tty1 run {{.Example}}</dt><dd class="dim">start a game</dd><dt>tty1 man {{.Example}}</dt><dd class="dim">read a game's manual page</dd><dt>tty1 doctor</dt><dd class="dim">check your terminal, and say what a better one would give you</dd></dl>
{{if index .Man "tty1"}}    <p class="dim note">Every command, and how a release is checked, is in <a href="/man/tty1">its manual page</a>.</p>
{{end}}  </section>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "manindex"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main" class="doc">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hot">The manual.</h1>
    <p class="about">Every page that comes home with a game, and tty1's own.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p><span class="dim">$</span> ls /usr/share/man</p>
    <p class="cols">{{range .Manuals}}<a href="/man/{{.Name}}">{{.Name}}({{.Section}})</a>{{end}}</p>
  </div>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "man"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main" class="doc">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hot">{{.Manual.Name}}({{.Manual.Section}})</h1>
    <p class="about">The manual page that comes home with <a href="/{{.Manual.Name}}">{{.Manual.Name}}</a> {{.Manual.Version}}.</p>
  </div>
  <p><span class="dim">$</span> tty1 man {{.Manual.Name}}</p>
  <div class="manual">{{.Manual.Body}}</div>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "arcade"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main" class="doc">
  <div>
    <h1 class="title"><img src="/media/arcade/name.svg" alt="arcade" width="{{namew "arcade" 0}}" height="80"></h1>
    <p class="about">The arcade is the studio's own server: the part of usr.games that lets two terminals play each other.</p>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>What it does today</h2>
    <p>It passes the moves of an online breakshot match between its two players, and keeps nothing once the match is over.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>What comes next</h2>
    <p class="dim">More is coming. Before each new part opens, this page will say what it keeps.</p>
  </section>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "terminals"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main" class="doc">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hot">Bring a good terminal.</h1>
    <p class="about">The games are drawn in the cells of your terminal, so the terminal is both the screen and the joystick. Most will play them. A good one plays them better.</p>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Keys you can hold</h2>
    <p>To walk and turn at once, a game has to know when you let go of a key. Terminals that speak the kitty keyboard protocol tell it:</p>
    <ul class="cols"><li>Ghostty</li><li>kitty</li><li>WezTerm</li><li>foot</li><li>iTerm2</li><li>Alacritty</li><li>Rio</li><li>Warp</li></ul>
    <p class="dim note">In the others only one key stays held at a time. Everything still plays. You just cannot walk and turn together.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>All the colours</h2>
    <p>The games paint in 24-bit colour where the terminal says it has it, and in the nearest of 256 colours where it does not.</p>
    <p class="dim note">Inside tmux or over ssh, the terminal's word often does not arrive. If the colours look banded there, this brings them back:</p>
    <p><span class="dim">$</span> export COLORTERM=truecolor</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>A big window</h2>
    <p>Every cell is two pixels, one above the other, so a bigger window or a smaller font is a sharper picture. 80 columns by 24 rows is enough to play. More is better.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Apple's Terminal</h2>
    <p>It works, with three differences. One key stays held at a time. 24-bit colour arrived in macOS 26, and before that it shows 256. And the picture is a little blockier: its half blocks would leave a faint seam, so the games draw whole cells there instead.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Check yours</h2>
    <p><span class="dim">$</span> tty1 doctor</p>
    <p class="dim note"><a href="/tty1">tty1</a> looks at the terminal it is running in and says what it found.</p>
  </section>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}

{{define "plan"}}{{template "head" .}}<main id="main" class="doc">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hot">The plan.</h1>
    <p class="about">What we are building, one part at a time. Newest first.</p>
    <p class="dim note">It is a feed too: <a href="/plan.xml">/plan.xml</a>.</p>
